From: Thierry Laurion <insurgo@riseup.net>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 18:52:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] xz: tune the x86 kernel-image LZMA2 preset

The x86 kernel image was packed with --lzma2=dict=32MiB at xz's default
parameters because scripts/xz_wrap.sh left LZMA2OPTS empty for the x86
case.  Set the x86 case to preset=9e,lc=4,lp=0,pb=1; the exec line still
appends ,dict=32MiB, so the level rides on the LZMA2 filter the same way
the initrd recipe does.

Why this must be a kernel patch: the kernel-image xz options are
hardcoded in scripts/xz_wrap.sh.  There is no Kconfig symbol, KCFLAGS or
environment hook to override them, so the only way to change the preset
is to patch the script itself.  (The initrd recipe is overridable via
INITRD_XZ_FILTER and is documented in doc/build-freshness.md; the
kernel image has no equivalent.)

Measured with xz 5.4.6 from the pinned tlaurion/heads-dev-env image on
the preboot payload (vmlinux.bin + vmlinux.relocs):
  t480        2,763,788 B -> 2,753,884 B  (-9,904 B)
  x230-max    2,789,692 B -> 2,764,580 B  (-25,112 B)
total -35,016 B.  mf/nice alternatives were measured and rejected; only
the x86 branch changes, all non-x86 branches are byte-identical.

Signed-off-by: Thierry Laurion <insurgo@riseup.net>
---
 scripts/xz_wrap.sh | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/xz_wrap.sh b/scripts/xz_wrap.sh
index 76e9cbcfbea..ae24ac7355c 100755
--- a/scripts/xz_wrap.sh
+++ b/scripts/xz_wrap.sh
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@
 LZMA2OPTS=
 
 case $SRCARCH in
-	x86)            BCJ=--x86 ;;
+	x86)            BCJ=--x86; LZMA2OPTS=preset=9e,lc=4,lp=0,pb=1 ;;
 	powerpc)        BCJ=--powerpc ;;
 	ia64)           BCJ=--ia64; LZMA2OPTS=pb=4 ;;
 	arm)            BCJ=--arm ;;
